      "definition": "Dārikapāda, the siddha to whom the manuscript (dārikapādānām, before the song) and the Tibetan heading attribute song 34. He names himself Dārika in 1b, the refrain, 4b and 5b; in 5b he owes his attainment to Lūyīpāda. Munidatta calls him a siddha master (cp.34.m1). Tibetan lives of the eighty-four siddhas make a Dārika a king who became Lūyī's disciple.",
      "symbolicImage": "",
      "symbolicReadings": [],
      "forbiddenInLine": [],
      "rationale": "The poet of song 34 needs a person entry; Dārikapāda follows the honorific form the manuscript uses, with Dārika, his self-naming in the song, as a variant."
    },
