      "definition": "Nondifference, being undivided (Sanskrit abheda; Old Bengali abhina, from abhinna): the inseparability tantric teaching claims for pairs such as emptiness and compassion, or wisdom and means. Song 34 opens with emptiness and compassion abhina; Munidatta speaks of taking the two, conventional and ultimate truth, as non-different (abhedopacāra) (cp.34.m2). The Tibetan has dbye ba med pa and dbyer med.",
      "symbolicImage": "",
      "symbolicReadings": [],
      "forbiddenInLine": [],
      "rationale": "The undividedness of emptiness and compassion is the doctrinal point of the opening line and recurs as the nondifference of wisdom and means; the noun takes \"nondifference\", the line's adjective \"undivided\"."
