      "matchRe": [],
      "definition": "The three emptinesses (śūnyatraya): in the Guhyasamāja completion stage, the empty, the very empty and the greatly empty, matched with three ever subtler luminous experiences, light, spreading of light and culmination of light; clear light, the all-empty, follows them. Munidatta reads the song's sky as 'the three emptinesses beginning with light', and its far shore as clear light (cp.34.m2).",
      "symbolicImage": "",
      "symbolicReadings": [],
      "forbiddenInLine": [],
      "rationale": "A technical term of completion-stage yoga that Munidatta uses to read the sky of the refrain; it ties together the existing entries for light, spreading of light and clear light."
