      "definition": "Non-abiding (Sanskrit apratiṣṭhāna; Old Bengali apaiṭhāna): resting neither in saṃsāra nor in a quiescent nirvāṇa, the Mahāyāna description of a buddha's nirvāṇa. Song 34 (3b) speaks of absorption in non-abiding great bliss; Munidatta has 'by the play of non-abiding great bliss' (cp.34.m4). The Tibetan comment has rab tu mi gnas pa, but the line reads rang gnas, 'own place'.",
