      "definition": "Non-arising (anutpāda): the Madhyamaka teaching that nothing truly comes into being, since nothing arises from itself, from another, from both or from neither; what does not arise does not cease. Munidatta says the unmarkable mind of the refrain is marked by non-arising (cp.34.m3); the Tibetan has ma skyes pa, 'unborn'. Compare arising (utpāda).",
