  "questions": [
    "gagana (new reading): Munidatta reads the sky in which Dārika plays as 'the three emptinesses beginning with light' (ālokādiśūnyatraya) (cp.34.m2); the Tibetan agrees (snang ba la sogs pa stong nyid gsum). Add this reading, and 'three emptinesses' to its never-in-line list?",
    "para (new reading and rendering): Munidatta says the far shore of that sky is clear light (prabhāsvara), full of great bliss (cp.34.m2; Tibetan de'i pha rol 'od gsal ba bde ba chen pos yongs su gang ba). Separately, para's English 'across' does not fit pārimakulem̐ in 1b and 2b, 'on the far shore'; may 'far shore' (or 'far') be added as a variant?",
    "karuna (new reading): Munidatta glosses compassion in 1a as conventional truth (saṃvṛtisatya) (cp.34.m2); the Tibetan comment has conventional bodhicitta (kun rdzob byang chub kyi sems) instead.",
    "sunyata (new reading): Munidatta glosses emptiness in 1a as the perfected form of that, ultimate truth (paramārthasatya) (cp.34.m2); the Tibetan agrees (de yongs su rdzogs pa'i gzugs don dam pa'i bden pa).",
    "indrajala (new reading): indījānī (4a) is filed under this entry on the strength of the Tibetan line (mig 'phrul dra ba). Munidatta's paraphrase instead has 'enjoy the sense objects and senses' (viṣayendriyopabhoga) (cp.34.m5; Tibetan yul dang dbang po nye bar longs spyod), reading indī- as indriya, as he does with indiāla in song 30. Record it as a reading of the entry?",
    "dari: its Tibetan form dA ri ka (from song 28) will tie with the poet's name in the Tibetan of 1b and 4b if it is a match form of dari. p-darika uses longer forms and a pattern for the bare name before a shad; please keep dA ri ka out of dari's match forms.",
    "thakura and raja: thakura records rgyal po as its Tibetan; if that is a match form it will tag the kings of 5a as the game piece. raja is therefore given no Tibetan match. Likewise rgyud (3a) is recorded for tantra as a form only, since tanti and santana already list it.",
    "raja: rāa (5a, 'other king') is recorded as a form but not matched, because the same spelling may stand for rāga elsewhere in the songs; only rāā and rāāre are matched.",
    "dhyana vs bhavana: jhāṇa (Tibetan bsam gtan) in 3a is dhyāna, not bhāvanā (sgom pa), which already holds 'meditation'. The new entry takes 'concentration' with 'meditation' as a variant; fold it into bhavana instead, or rename bhavana 'cultivation'?",
    "dvadasa-bhumi: the line's bhuaṇa means 'worlds' (as in tiṇi bhuaṇa), while Munidatta reads twelve stages (bhūmi) and the Tibetan line has ten stages (sa bcu), its comment the twelfth stage. The entry follows the stages and keeps 'twelve worlds' as a variant; which should the line use?"
  ],
